======================================================================
  D. WHY THE ALMOST-DAG? (Walsh even-order connection)
======================================================================

  Iso class graph edges: 30
  H-increasing: 29
  H-decreasing: 0
  H-level: 1

  WHY ALMOST-DAG:
  H has only even Walsh orders (0, 2, 4).
  Order-2 dominates (94.7% of Var(H) at n=5).
  An arc flip changes H by: delta = 2*sum of order-2 + order-4 terms.
  Since order-2 >> order-4, most flips have definite sign => DAG-like.
  Level edges occur when order-2 and order-4 contributions cancel.
  At n=5: 1 level edge(s) out of 30 total (3.3%).

